course: dictionary
lesson: 2654
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To work out which one is meant, look at the context: the other words and what the text is about. «Deuce» is a good example.
explain: In tennis, «at 40-40 (deuce) you need two points in a row» to win the game. Deuce means the score is level, with both players on 40 points. Words like «love» and «game» also tell you the text is about sport.
explain: In card games, deuce means a card with two spots. Look for clues like cards, a deck or a hand of cards. Without a clue like that, the word could mean something else.
explain: In old stories, «what the deuce?» is an old-fashioned way of showing surprise or annoyance. Check the other words first, and if you are still unsure, look the word up in a dictionary.
fact: A word can have more than one meaning, so always check the context to find the right one.
fact: In tennis, «deuce» is the score when both players have 40 points, so the game is level.
fact: At deuce, a player must win two points in a row to win the game.
fact: «Deuce» can also be a playing card or a dice face with two spots.
fact: In old-fashioned exclamations like «what the deuce?», it is a mild word for the devil, used to show surprise or annoyance.
exercise: «Tennis points go 0 (love), 15, 30, 40, game; at 40-40 (deuce) you need two points in a row.» What does deuce mean in this sentence? | A mild word for the devil | A mistake in the game | A playing card with two spots | *A score where both players have 40 points
exercise: «The cards were shuffled, and Mia found the deuce.» What does deuce most likely mean here? | A ball that has gone out of play | *A playing card with two spots | The score in a tennis game | A mild word for the devil
exercise: «What the deuce?» shouted Dad, when he saw the broken window. What does deuce show? | That Dad is holding a card | That the score is level | *Surprise or annoyance, in an old-fashioned way | That the window is two metres wide
test: «At 40-all, which is deuce, you need two points in a row to win.» Why does deuce mean the score is level? | Both players have 15 points | One player has already won the game | *Both players have 40 points | The players have stopped playing
test: In «Leo dealt the cards and laid down a deuce», which word is the clue that deuce means a playing card? | *cards | laid | down | Leo
exam: Which meaning of deuce fits a tennis match where the score is 40-all? | *The score is level, with both players on 40 points | An old-fashioned word for the devil | A playing card with a king on it | A ball that has gone out of play
